---
// Privacy Policy (2026-11-05). Every statement maps to the data inventory taken from the site's code: the
// four forms (ContactForm.astro, NewsletterForm.astro, the Code559 notify form), the Apps Script handler
// (docs/apps-script-form-handler.gs), worksheet storage in public/scripts/site.js, and the build scan that
// found script.google.com as the only outside host. No statute is claimed. Owner-only values come from
// site.legal in src/config/site.ts; until all are set, LegalStatus shows the review banner.
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import LegalStatus from "@/components/LegalStatus.astro";
import LegalValue from "@/components/LegalValue.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site, sitePath } from "@/config/site";

const { legal } = site;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | 559 Solutions"
  description="The Privacy Policy for the 559 Solutions website: what the forms collect, where it is stored, what is not collected, and your choices."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Privacy Policy" }]} />
      <p class="eyebrow">Site information</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">What this site collects, why, and where it goes.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="section">
    <article class="narrow legal-content">
      <LegalStatus />

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This site is run by <LegalValue value={legal.legalName} />, doing business as 559 Solutions ("we" or "us"). For
        privacy questions or requests, email <LegalValue value={legal.privacyEmail} kind="email" /> or write to{" "}
        <LegalValue value={legal.businessAddress} />.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>The site collects information about you only through its forms. Each form collects the following.</p>
      <section class="table-scroll legal-table-wrap" aria-label="What each form collects" tabindex="0">
        <table class="legal-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Form</th>
              <th scope="col">Where it appears</th>
              <th scope="col">What it collects</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Contact form</th>
              <td><a href={sitePath("/contact/")}>Contact page</a></td>
              <td>Name, email, organization (optional), inquiry type, message, and your consent</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Article email signup</th>
              <td>Articles and the <a href={sitePath("/subscribe/")}>Subscribe page</a></td>
              <td>Email, the page you signed up on, and your consent</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Release waitlist</th>
              <td>Pages for resources that are not released yet</td>
              <td>Email, the page you signed up on, and your consent</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Code559 course notice</th>
              <td><a href={sitePath("/code559/")}>Code559 page</a></td>
              <td>First name, email, the course you chose, and your consent</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>
      <p>Along with what you type, a submission can include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the address of the page you were on;</li>
        <li>a short label that names the form, such as "newsletter:the-hero-trap";</li>
        <li>the date and time it was received.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Each form also has a hidden field that people do not see. It catches automated spam. If that field is filled in,
        the submission is not saved.
      </p>

      <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
      <p>
        Worksheet and self-check answers stay in your browser. They are not sent to us. If you tick "Save on this device"
        on a worksheet, your answers are stored only in that browser, so they are there when you come back. Untick the box
        to remove them. Answers leave your browser only if you copy or print them yourself.
      </p>
      <p>Quiz answers ("Make the call") are checked in your browser and are not sent anywhere.</p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To reply to messages sent through the contact form.</li>
        <li>
          To send the emails each form describes, and nothing else: an email when a new article is published, one email when
          a resource is released, or one email when a Code559 course opens.
        </li>
        <li>To keep a record that you gave consent.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
      <p>
        Forms send what you enter to a Google Apps Script web app that runs in our Google account. The script adds one row
        to a Google Sheet. Google stores it as our service provider. Google's handling is described in the{" "}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The script does not send email. We send the emails people sign up for using{" "}
        <LegalValue value={legal.emailTool} />.
      </p>

      <h2>Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        Digital products are sold through Gumroad. You check out on Gumroad, not on this site. We receive the information
        Gumroad provides to sellers about a purchase. Gumroad's privacy policy applies to checkout:{" "}
        <LegalValue value={legal.gumroadPrivacyUrl} kind="url">Gumroad Privacy Policy</LegalValue>.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics, cookies and browser storage</h2>
      <p>
        This site has no analytics. The site's pages and scripts set no cookies. The only browser storage the site uses is
        the worksheet "Save on this device" option described above.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our web host may keep server logs of requests to the site. <LegalValue value={legal.hostingLogs} /> The resource and
        article filters put your filter choice in the page address, so it can appear in those logs. Search text is never
        put in the address.
      </p>

      <h3>Other companies a page contacts</h3>
      <p>
        Pages on this site load no scripts, fonts, images or embedded content from other companies. Only one outside host
        is contacted, and only when you submit a form:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>script.google.com</strong> (Google) receives what you entered in the form, plus your IP address and
          browser details that come with any web request. Our script does not write your IP address to the sheet.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When you follow a link to another site, your browser may tell that site you came from this one. What that site
        collects is covered by its own policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell or rent your information. We share it only with the service providers named on this page (Google,
        Gumroad, our email tool and our web host), or when the law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p><LegalValue value={legal.dataRetention} /></p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          To stop getting emails, reply to any email from us, or use the <a href={sitePath("/contact/")}>contact form</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          To ask for a copy of your information, or to have it corrected or deleted, email{" "}
          <LegalValue value={legal.privacyEmail} kind="email" />.
        </li>
        <li>To remove saved worksheet answers, untick "Save on this device" or clear your browser's site data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect information from children under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps to protect what you send us. No method of sending or storing information is perfectly
        secure.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If we change this policy, we will post the new version here with a new effective date.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
